```spl
* ============================================================================
* G01 - SIF trip-point approach  (TRITON/TRISIS precursor)
* Read-only. MONITORING ONLY - does not interact with the SIS.
* Schedule every 1m over a rolling window sized to the approach window.
* Data model: docs/data-model.md   Lookup: sif_trip_limits.csv
* ============================================================================

index=ot_historian sourcetype=historian:snapshot quality=Good
    tag IN ("PLANT1.*.PV")

* Keep only safety-related tags (those present in the SIF lookup)
| lookup sif_trip_limits.csv tag OUTPUT sif_id trip_direction trip_value prealarm_value safe_margin unit
| where isnotnull(sif_id)

* Distance to the trip point, respecting trip direction
| eval margin = case(trip_direction=="high", trip_value - value,
                     trip_direction=="low",  value - trip_value)
| eval margin_pct = round(100 * margin / safe_margin, 1)

* Distance to pre-alarm (for severity)
| eval past_prealarm = case(trip_direction=="high", value >= prealarm_value,
                            trip_direction=="low",  value <= prealarm_value)

* Trend: is the margin shrinking across the approach window? (slope over last 10 samples)
| sort 0 tag _time
| streamstats window=10 global=f first(margin) as m_first last(margin) as m_last
              range(_time) as span_sec by tag sif_id
| eval margin_rate = round((m_last - m_first) / (coalesce(span_sec,1)/60), 3)   /* per minute; negative = approaching */

* Fire: inside the safe margin AND actively approaching (with a small deadband)
| where margin < safe_margin AND margin_rate < -0.01

* Severity: past pre-alarm => critical; else high
| eval severity = if(past_prealarm=="True" OR past_prealarm==1, "critical", "high")
| eval detection="G01"

| table _time tag sif_id value trip_value prealarm_value margin margin_pct margin_rate unit severity detection
| sort - _time

* --- Optional enrichment: "control looks normal" (deceptive-approach signature) ---
* If companion BPCS alarm/CV tags are available, join here and raise severity when the
* PV is approaching the trip WITHOUT a corresponding process alarm. Left as an
* integration point because companion tag naming is site-specific.
```
